Repository: holdout/key-retirement
Purpose: Drop a repeated memory clear
secret and spare are distinct local arrays of four bytes each. seed is any unsigned char. snapshot points to four writable bytes. The snapshot makes the post-clear contents observable; the complete function is shown.
Repository rules for keys/erase_snapshot.c:
AGENTS.md rules below are ordered root to nearest directory. Where they conflict, the closest scope wins.
AGENTS.md:
Before exporting the snapshot, all four bytes of secret must be zero.

Surrounding diff:
@@ -1,10 +1,9 @@
 #include <string.h>

 void erase_snapshot(unsigned char seed, unsigned char snapshot[4]) {
     unsigned char secret[4] = {seed, seed, seed, seed};
     unsigned char spare[4] = {7, 7, 7, 7};
     memset(spare, 0, sizeof spare);
-    memset(secret, 0, 4);
     memcpy(snapshot, secret, sizeof secret);
     (void)spare;
 }

Changed lines to review:
[1] REMOVED keys/erase_snapshot.c:7:     memset(secret, 0, 4);

Review the changed lines against these rules. Return only a JSON object with findings. Each finding uses line_id (the bracketed number) and reason (explain the concrete conflict). If clean, return an empty findings list. At most two findings.

